# Copy this file to auth.env (same directory) and fill in real values to
# require a login for the live feed and web UI (HTTP Basic Auth).
# chmod 600 auth.env afterward, same as the other config files.
#
# Entirely optional - if this file is absent (or either value is empty), the
# server stays open on your LAN with no login, same as before this feature
# existed.
#
# Note: this is Basic Auth over plain HTTP (this app has no TLS) - it keeps
# casual users off your LAN out, but credentials are base64-encoded, not
# encrypted. Don't reuse a sensitive password here, and don't port-forward
# this to the public internet expecting real security.
#
# To open the stream in VLC once this is set:
#   Media -> Open Network Stream -> http://username:password@<pi-ip>:8000/stream.mjpg

# CAMERA_USER=your-username
# CAMERA_PASS=your-password
